{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>A man of short</b> — two joined. That is: he fears HaShem and turns from evil, and the fool is provoked and grows angry with others, and trusts that he will live; and one who is short of temper is provoked at all times by a deed of folly." "<b>And a man of schemes</b> — evil thoughts, he is hated, for HaShem hates him."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:45.581318200Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}